// SE 1.5.97 store-site tables. DRAFT generated by findings/swf-stores-work/gen.py from scan_stores.py and
// scan_fade.py. Every entry's bytes are verified before anything is patched.
//
// The hidden-store table comes from the same program-wide scan as AE 1.6.1170 (scan_stores.py reproduces
// the AE table exactly): Ghidra-disassembled writes to `[reg + 0xf4]`:
//  - every `or` that may set bit 0;
//  - every `and` that may clear it;
//  - every `mov` of any width (the stub compares bit 0 itself).
// As on AE, `add`/`inc` counters are not in the table (UNCONFIRMED: the AE header lists one add and one
// inc but the AE table has neither; SE has one add and two inc, listed commented out at the end).
// Some sites are not an NiAVObject's (stack slots, other classes); their events carry keys no scene
// object has. Two RSP-based sites (in .bind) are left out, because the stub's call moves RSP.
// SE codegen differs from AE: where AE computes the new flags in a register and stores them with one
// `mov`, SE usually branches to an `or [r+0xf4], 1` and an `and [r+0xf4], 0xfffffffe`, so many AE sites
// become two SE sites (see findings/swf-stores.md).
// Main::Draw's and TESWaterReflections::Update's stores hide a node and show it again within one frame, around views (the
// first-person skeleton; the water shapes and the player's 3D). They are kept, one event per store, and never merged or dropped:
// see the README's "Hides within a frame".
// Comments name the SE function (Ghidra name; the AE counterpart in parentheses where SE has no name) and
// the instruction (dword unless stated).
//
// Table order is the event's site index; keep it stable within a release.
